        "stepByStepSolution": "Step 1: Identify given parameters:\nEffort (E) = 250 N\nDistance moved by Effort (d_E) = 4.0 m\nLoad (L) = 800 N\nDistance moved by Load (d_L) = 1.0 m\nStep 2: Calculate Work Input (W_in):\nFormula: Work Input = Effort × Distance moved by Effort\nW_in = 250 N × 4.0 m = 1,000 J.\nStep 3: Calculate Work Output (W_out):\nFormula: Work Output = Load × Distance moved by Load\nW_out = 800 N × 1.0 m = 800 J.\nStep 4: Calculate Mechanical Advantage (MA):\nFormula: MA = Load / Effort\nMA = 800 N / 250 N = 3.2 (dimensionless ratio).\nStep 5: Calculate Velocity Ratio (VR):\nFormula: VR = Distance moved by Effort / Distance moved by Load\nVR = 4.0 m / 1.0 m = 4.0 (dimensionless ratio).\nStep 6: Calculate Efficiency (η):\nMethod A (Work Energy Ratio): η = (Work Output / Work Input) × 100% = (800 J / 1,000 J) × 100% = 80%.\nMethod B (Advantage Ratio): η = (MA / VR) × 100% = (3.2 / 4.0) × 100% = 80%.\nStep 7: Calculate Wasted Energy:\nWasted Energy = Work Input - Work Output = 1,000 J - 800 J = 200 J (dissipated as thermal friction and lifting pulley frame).",
