        "stepByStepSolution": "Step 1: Calculate the Velocity Ratio (VR):\nFormula: VR = Length of Slope (L) / Vertical Height (h)\nVR = 6.0 m / 1.5 m = 4.0.\nStep 2: Calculate the Mechanical Advantage (MA):\nFormula: MA = Load / Effort\nMA = 900 N / 300 N = 3.0.\nStep 3: Calculate Mechanical Efficiency (η):\nFormula: η = (MA / VR) × 100% = (3.0 / 4.0) × 100% = 75%.\nStep 4: Calculate Work Input and Work Output:\nWork Input = Effort × Slope Length = 300 N × 6.0 m = 1,800 J.\nWork Output = Load × Vertical Height = 900 N × 1.5 m = 1,350 J.\nStep 5: Determine Work done against friction and frictional force:\nWasted energy (Work against friction, W_f) = Work Input - Work Output = 1,800 J - 1,350 J = 450 J.\nSince W_f = F_f × Distance moved along slope (6.0 m):\nF_f = W_f / L = 450 J / 6.0 m = 75 N.",
